# The DataFlash Logs page: tableLayoutPanel2, whose Download DataFlash Log Via Mavlink opens the
# Log Downloader and whose Review a Log opens the log browser.
#
# The Log Downloader's Log_Load asks the vehicle for its list - or, with no vehicle, says "Please
# connect your drone" in its output. Download Selected Logs with nothing checked says to check
# some; Download All Logs with nothing listed asks for the list again. The form's close box
# closes it. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1204-1209, 1380-1385, Log/LogDownloadMavLink.cs:51-89,
# 158-197, 428-448, Log/LogStrings.resx`
#
# Needs no link: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-dataflash.gui

# A data directory of its own: the machine's config.xml remembers the last link, and the
# application opens it when it is started without one.
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 14
# No link was given: nothing has arrived.
expect link.frames 0

# DataFlash Logs is the last header: bring it to the front of the row, then show its page.
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
expect fly.tabs.first 13
click fly-tab-logbrowse
expect fly.tab tablogbrowse
expect fly.page.overflow 0

click fly-dfmavlink
expect fly.logs.open true
expect fly.logs.output Please connect your drone
expect fly.logs.items 0

click fly-logs-dlthese
expect fly.logs.output Please select some logs by checking the check boxes in the list
click fly-logs-dlall
expect fly.logs.output Please connect your drone
expect fly.logs.fetching none

click fly-logs-close
expect fly.logs.open false

# Review a Log: the log browser, which is a screen of its own here.
click fly-logbrowse
expect screen logs
